## intro

So, I created this website a while to ago to track my PhD and my work as a geology researcher at Unicamp. But as life happens, I'm only updating this now. But anyway, I just wrapped up the first week of a Petrochronology (Petrochron) papers that I'm
taking, by Prof. Vinícius T. Meira. I will also talk about other topics from this first year at some poits, I guess.

The Petrochronology class will have two weeks. Here is a summary of the first week:

### day 1: Intro to Petrochronology

The first day of the course was an introduction to some concepts and the main body of work on Petrochronology. A good first reading in these is of course the review volume from *Khon, Lanari and Engi (2017) - Petrochronology: Methods and Applications*.


A nice quote from this work:

> ...a rock does not have, sensu stricto, one age

### day 2: Analytical Techniques in Petrochronology

The first part of the day was a recap on main mapping techniques used in Petrochron, specially SEM and EPMA. I learned about the ways that electron beams interact with samples and how chemical information is detected with EDS and WDS spectometes.

